This machine's opened firewall ports (PengyOS).

/etc/nftables.conf includes every *.nft file here into the input chain of
its default-deny firewall. Each file holds input-chain rule statements, e.g.

    tcp dport 8086 ip saddr 10.0.23.0/24 ct state new accept

Manage them with pengyos-firewall instead of by hand:

    pengyos-firewall status
    sudo pengyos-firewall allow 8086 --from 10.0.23.0/24
    sudo pengyos-firewall remove 8086 --from 10.0.23.0/24

/etc survives OS updates, and so do these files. They add to the image's
ruleset without replacing /etc/nftables.conf, so the image can still update
that file. This README is not a .nft file, so the firewall ignores it.
